<card id="c" title="What&apos;s on My Raspberry Pi 5">
<do type="prev" label="Back"><prev/></do>
<p>Next, <b>nginx</b> on the Raspberry Pi receives the requests and proxies them to the appropriate Raspberry Pi ports.</p>
<p>But that&apos;s not all.</p>
<p><b>Home Media Server</b></p>
<p>At the same time, my <b>Raspberry Pi 5</b> is used as a home media server.</p>
<p>Since the rented apartment has an old, inexpensive TV without the ability to install apps, I connected the <b>Raspberry Pi</b> to it, which is where the graphical interface comes in handy.</p>
<p>Thus, you can watch movies, listen to music, and browse YouTube right from the couch.</p>
